Development combined-kernel boot smoke, 2026-11-15 UTC
ISO SHA256 f3d084a185f8771316b4ea7a6b24f16804407ed3214a8481b5e8a606e9c724d1
This is an early integration checkpoint, not the final release hash.

PASS: BIOS32 (qemu64,-lm,-pae), IA32 UEFI (qemu64,-lm), AMD64 UEFI (qemu64).
All use QEMU pc/TCG,128MiB, standard VGA, copied ZeroFS data and private OVMF
variables. The optical ISO is read-only. BIOS32 genuinely lacks both LM/PAE.
Each reached the new A:|> prompt within40 seconds, mounted ZeroFS and completed
discovery. PS/2 injection ran disks, go a:|, watch, info, tasks. Only the
writable ATA ZeroFS volume was listed; the ATAPI optical boot medium was not.
The explicit root was accepted, watch showed the expected empty data disk,
and both graphics/compute workers remained runnable with nonzero counters.
All three800x600 screenshots were inspected: original portrait, desktop,
terminal and worker status are visible. All three VMs were stopped.

Finding sent to parent: disks ends its listing with LF alone. The console
retains its previous column, so the following prompt is visibly indented.
Serial confirms `ZeroFS\nA:|>` rather than CRLF. Fix belongs to the kernel's
formatter/console, outside this agent's owned boot sources. No boot capacity,
stack-pool or architecture transition failure was found.

Evidence: MODE.serial, MODE.status, MODE.png and MODE.qemu in this directory.
run-smoke.sh records exact VM arguments and keyboard automation.
inputs.sha256 records the copied ISO and unchanged original data images.
